C(103,'External internal-Hom Künneth',[103,106,107],
'For bounded constructible finite-Tor F,F′ on X and G,G′ on Y, over a separably closed field with invertible torsion coefficients, the canonical exterior-product comparison RHom(F,F′)⊠ᴸRHom(G,G′)→RHom(F⊠ᴸG,F′⊠ᴸG′) is an isomorphism in the applicable étale duality formalism.',
'open on the pages','A','The manuscript puts this at the heart of the reverse map and explicitly proposes a proof via resolution. Illusie2026 records the later finiteness input removing resolution in SGA5 II/III. Exact target D+/D− scope after deletion is not identifiable here; the bounded finite-Tor statement is the safe reconstruction, not an assertion that every displayed unbounded version is proved.',['Illusie2026:§2–4','MilneLEC:22.3,24.3'],['P2-S01'],'Modern safe hypotheses deliberately narrower than the unresolved manuscript target.',confidence='medium')
